   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Parental",
   "texto": [
    "**Bunic** and **bunică** mean «Grandpa.» and «Grandma.»; **verișor** and **verișoară**, «cousin» and «prima». **Cumnat** and **cumnată** are «brother-in-law» and «sister-in-law»."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The genius.",
   "texto": [
    "To say «of whom», the possessed name usually brings the article to the end and the family member changes: **sora mamei** («the mother's sister»). feminine names like Ana appear **-ei** (**soțul Anei**); masculine names are used as **lui** (**fratele lui Paul**). «de» is not added as in Spanish."
   ]
  },
